# Ebb — Seats

## Contract

The seat contract — what a seat is, its lifecycle, seat accounting, the rules, and running one — is `contracts/SEATS.md` in the template repo, copied verbatim into `wheelhouse/fleet/SEATS.md` at install. It is not reproduced here, and it is not edited per-project.

This specimen shows only what the interview writes: the roster below, and the seats that were offered and turned down.

## This project

### Roster

One line per seat, mirroring `seats/seats.json` — the machine record, which decides; this table is the human record and must agree with it. Agent directories land under `$HOME/.pi-seats-ebb/` (namespace `ebb`, recorded as `namespace=ebb` in `wheelhouse/.template-source`). Each model was pinned per seat from the selected harness's own live listing or binding probe at install (BOOTSTRAP question 8's read-back table), not from a remembered family. Harness and auth route are durable columns question 8 also fills; auth route names a route, never a credential.

| Seat | Role brief | Harness | Provider | Model | Auth route | Agent directory |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| `worker-1` | `wheelhouse/fleet/WORKER.md` | `claude-code` | `anthropic` | `claude-sonnet-5` | `oauth` | `~/.pi-seats-ebb/worker-1` |
| `reviewer` | `wheelhouse/crew/REVIEWER.md` | `codex` | `openai-codex` | `gpt-5.6-sol` | `oauth` | `~/.pi-seats-ebb/reviewer` — never authors what it reviews, so its directory differs from every worker's |
| `verifier` | `wheelhouse/crew/VERIFIER.md` consumer-surface walker | `pi` | `openrouter` | `z-ai/glm-5.3-flash` | `api_key` | `~/.pi-seats-ebb/verifier` — walks ISA claim surfaces via `seats/walk.ts`; gates claims, not beads |
| (commander) | this folder's `CLAUDE.md` | external | — | — | — | none: the principal's own session, `"external": true` in the roster |

### Declined seats

| Seat | Reason | Date |
|---|---|---|
| Designer | "I want to decompose the first few beads myself so I learn what a good one looks like." | 2026-08-14 |
| Second worker | One reviewer, one worker — take it when the reviewer starts waiting. | 2026-08-14 |

Each of these was offered seat by seat at install and turned down. A second worker goes in when the reviewer is idle waiting for work; the designer goes in when the principal is spending more time decomposing beads than deciding direction.

### Walk cadence

The cadence value lives in `wheelhouse/INTEGRATOR.md`'s project half, not here. This install accepted the template default `walk_cadence_merges: 5`; claim-closing walks use the surface named by the claim, and every-5 drift walks use the primary surface named in `wheelhouse/crew/VERIFIER.md`.

---

## What the installed file actually looks like

This specimen shows only the generated half. The file at `wheelhouse/fleet/SEATS.md` in a real project is:

```
# Fleet: Seats
<intro line>

## Contract                 <- copied verbatim from contracts/SEATS.md, never edited
  ### What a seat is        <- persistent seats, plus verify.ts REVIEWER and walk.ts VERIFIER one-shots
  ### Lifecycle             <- persistent context is a cache; session survives stop/resume
  ### Seat accounting       <- one seat = one subscription = one human beneficiary
  ### Rules
  ### Running a seat        <- one paragraph, pointing at seats/README.md
  ### Minimum viable fleet

## This project             <- everything from here down is generated, and is the
  ### Roster                   only part this specimen shows
  ### Declined seats
```

If your installed file is missing the contract half, the install split it in the wrong place. That has happened; see the note in `BOOTSTRAP.md` about matching the heading exactly.
